# Kookapp — product & stack

- **Spec**: `kookapp_plan_v2.html` is the source of truth. Read the relevant section before implementing a feature or changing the data model.
- **Stack**: Expo (React Native), Expo Router, `expo-sqlite`, `expo-secure-store`, Claude API (Haiku default; Sonnet where the plan says).
- **Language**: All **user-visible** UI strings in **Dutch**. Keep code identifiers/comments in English unless the user prefers otherwise.
- **Privacy**: Local SQLite only; no user accounts; no cloud DB. AI calls use **minimal context** (e.g. one recipe for import/tips/edit) — **never** the full recipe collection.
- **Secrets**: API key only from Settings, stored with **expo-secure-store**; never hardcode; never commit keys (no `.env` with real keys in git).
- **Offline**: Cooking flow (view, checkboxes, timers, scaling), local search, and shopping aggregation must work **without internet**. AI actions: check connectivity; if offline, disable + short Dutch explanation.
- **Build order**: Implement plan features **1 → 10** in order unless the user explicitly reprioritizes. Skip items marked **later** (voice, Nextcloud WebDAV export, etc.) until asked.
- **Scope**: Prefer one milestone per change set (e.g. “feature 2 only”). Avoid drive-by refactors unrelated to the task.
